R"VG(
# news7.vg (H-04's second pass): the news's register, continued: the rule (a ruler's death, an accession, a resignation, a new
# constitution), a death of note, the unrest and the move to the cities.

# ---- the rule --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

news.rulerdeath
  {news.h.rd}\n{news.rd.m} {news.rd.x}
news.h.rd
  {$e.a:full} is dead
  (has:$e.a.title) The {$e.a.title} is dead
  Mourning
news.rd.m
  {$e.a:full} died yesterday at {$e.place}, aged {#$e.a.age}. The nation is in mourning.
  (has:$e.a.epithet has:$e.a.reigned) {$e.a:name} {$e.a.epithet} died at {$e.place} in the {#$e.a.reigned:ord} year of the reign, aged {#$e.a.age}.
  (has:$e.a.reigned) {$e.a:full} is dead at {#$e.a.age}, after a reign of {#$e.a.reigned|year}.
  (has:$e.a.epithet) {$e.a:name} {$e.a.epithet} is dead at {$e.place}, aged {#$e.a.age}, and the bells have not stopped since.
news.rd.x
  The shops will close for {n} days and the bells will be rung at noon.
  The body will lie in state at {$seat}, where the queues already reach the river.
  Black cloth hangs from the windows of {$home}, and {colour.mourn} ribbons on the doors.
  The theatres are closed and the papers, this one included, are printed with black borders.
  The {herd} of the royal farms have been led through {streets.of} with {colour.mourn} on their horns.

news.accession
  (has:$e.a) {news.h.acc}\n{news.acc.m} {news.said} that {news.acc.t}.
  (!has:$e.a) Change at the top\nThe rule has passed into new hands at {$seat}. {news.said} that {news.acc.t}.
news.h.acc
  A new head of state
  {$e.a:name} takes office
  Change at the top
news.acc.m
  {$e.a:full} has taken office at {$seat}, {news.acc.how}.
  ($e.accession=elected) {$e.a:full} has been elected {news.margin}, {news.acc.how}.
  ($e.accession=elected) The votes are counted, and {$e.a:full} has won {news.margin}; the losers have gone home to {news.losers}.
  ($e.accession=seized|$e.accession=revolution) {$e.a:full} has taken the rule, and the old ministers have left {$seat} in a hurry.
  ($e.accession=inherited) {$e.a:full} has come to the throne, and the oaths will be taken at {$seat} on the rest day.
news.acc.t
  there would be no changes
  the old ministers would stay
  the taxes would not rise this year
  order would be kept
  the roads would be mended at last
  the new reign would be one of peace and of bread

news.ruleend
  {news.h.re}\n{$e.a:full} [has given up the rule|has stepped down|is no longer at the head of affairs]. {news.said} that the reasons were [private|of health|plain to everyone].
news.h.re
  Resignation
  The end of a reign
  {$e.a:name} goes

news.government
  {news.h.gov}\n{news.gov.m} {news.said} that order would be kept.
news.h.gov
  A new constitution
  The old order ends
news.gov.m
  The form of the rule has changed.
  ($e.gov=republic) The crown is abolished and the consuls will govern.
  ($e.gov=assembly) The Assembly will govern from today, and every town will send its delegate.
  ($e.gov=corporate) The companies have taken over the running of the state, which some say they always had.
  ($e.gov=council) A council will rule, and nobody will rule alone.

news.death
  {news.h.death}\n{news.death.m} {news.death.x}
news.h.death
  Death of {$e.a:name}
  {$e.a:name}
news.death.m
  {$e.a:full} died at {$e.place}, aged {#$e.a.age}.
  (has:$e.a.trade) {$e.a:full}, {$e.a.trade}, died at {$e.place} at the age of {#$e.a.age}.
  (has:$e.a.trade) The death is announced of {$e.a:full}, for many years a {$e.a.trade} at {$e.place}, {news.deathhow}.
news.death.x
  The funeral will be at {deadplace}, {time.of}.
  Many at {$e.place} will remember {$e.a:obj}.
  (has:$e.a.trait) {$e.a:name} was [known as|thought|remembered as] a {$e.a.trait} [soul|neighbour|presence] by those who knew {$e.a:obj}.
  The {craft} works of {$e.place} will stop for an hour on the day of the funeral.

# ---- unrest and moving ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

news.unrest
  ($e.unrest=strike) Strike at {$e.place}\n{news.strike.m} {news.strike.t}
  ($e.unrest=bread|$e.unrest=riot) Riot at {$e.place}\n{news.riot.m} {#$e.value:about} dead.
  ($e.unrest=rising) Rising at {$e.place}\nArmed men have taken the town hall at {$e.place}.
news.strike.m
  The {news.strikers} at {$e.place} have stopped work {news.strike.why}.
  Work has stopped at the {craft} works of {$e.place}, where the hands want {n} {smallcoin} more a day and the owners want them back at work.
news.strike.t
  The owners, {news.owners}, have [refused to meet them|offered half of what was asked|sent for the police].
  The strikers are holding meetings in {town.open} and singing the old songs to new words.
  The {crop} for the town is rotting in the yards.
  The wives of the strikers are keeping them in {food}, and the shops are keeping them in credit.
news.riot.m
  Troops were called to {$e.place} last night after crowds broke the windows of the bakeries.
  The price of {food} brought the women of {$e.place} into the streets, and the soldiers did not know what to do with them.

news.migration
  (has:$e.place has:$e.place2) To the cities\n{#$e.value:about} more have left {$e.place} for {$e.place2} this year, the council reports.
  (!has:$e.place has:$e.place2) To the cities\n{#$e.value:about} more have left the countryside for {$e.place2} this year, the council reports. The villages are full of the old.
  (!has:$e.place2) The young leave\n{#$e.value:about} have left the countryside for the cities this year, the council reports.
news.acc.how
  with the oaths taken in {holyplace}
  quietly, on a rest day
  to the sound of {instrument}
  before a crowd that filled {town.open}
news.strikers
  workers
  men at the yards
  weavers
  {craft} hands
  carters
  women of the {craft} sheds
  (coast=1) dockers
news.strike.why
  over the wages
  over the hours
  after an accident at the {news.machine}
  because the ration of {food} was cut
  until the foreman goes
news.machine
  looms
  presses
  furnace
  vats
news.owners
  who live in {city}
  three brothers and a widow
  a company from over the sea
  the family that gave {holyplace} its bells
  who have not been seen at the works in years
news.margin
  by a clear margin
  by {n} votes in every hundred
  on the second count
  unopposed, which nobody remembers happening before
  by the narrowest of margins, after a recount
news.losers
  count again
  write letters to this paper
  their {herd}
  think about next time
news.deathhow
  at a great age
  after a short illness
  peacefully, at home
  in {season.any}, as {$e.a:name} would have wished
)VG"
